  "summary": "Assam Pani Meteka Craft, also known as Water hyacinth craft, is an emerging cottage and handicraft industry in the Indian state of Assam.",
  "description": "Assam Pani Meteka Craft, also known as Water hyacinth craft, is an emerging cottage and handicraft industry in the Indian state of Assam. The craft uses Pani Meteka (water hyacinth), an invasive aquatic plant, as its primary raw material to produce a wide range of eco-friendly and biodegradable products such as handbags, yoga mats, baskets, furniture items, and household utilities. The craft has gained recognition for its role in sustainable livelihood generation, particularly among rural women and fishing communities.\n\nIn 2024, Assam Pani Meteka Craft received Geographical Indication (GI) registration under the name Assam Pani Meteka Craft, recognizing its uniqueness and traditional association with the region.",
  "culturalContext": "Registered as a Geographical Indication of India (handicraft, Assam; registration 2023–24), which protects the name for products made in its place of origin by traditional methods.",
